 "DNG (Digital Negative) is Adobe's open RAW format, published in 2004 as a standardized alternative to the zoo of proprietary camera formats. Some cameras write DNG natively — Leica, Pentax, Ricoh, DJI drones, most Blackmagic cinema cameras — and Lightroom can convert any proprietary RAW into DNG for archival.": "dng-to-jpg,dng-to-png,dng-to-webp",
 "Being open does not make DNG files any easier to share: they are still raw sensor data, still large, and still ignored by anything that isn't photo software. If you archived your library as DNG and now need web-ready images, a converter is the bridge.": "dng-to-jpg,dng-to-png,dng-to-webp",
 "ShiftRaw converts DNG to JPG in your browser with no upload. The LibRaw engine handles both linear and mosaic DNG variants, and your files never leave your device.": "dng-to-jpg",
 "How to convert DNG to JPG": "dng-to-jpg",
