 "Why convert RAF to JPG?": "raf-to-jpg",
 "RAF is Fujifilm's RAW format, and Fujifilm is the interesting outlier in the RAW world: since 2012 its X-series cameras use X-Trans sensors with a 6×6 color filter array that deliberately avoids the Bayer pattern, trading demosaicing simplicity for reduced moiré and stronger color fidelity.": "raf-to-jpg,raf-to-png,raf-to-webp",
 "That unusual sensor design is why RAF files need specific processing — generic converters that assume Bayer data render X-Trans files soft or artifacted. ShiftRaw's LibRaw engine includes proper X-Trans interpolation, so your files get the full-resolution treatment they deserve.": "raf-to-jpg,raf-to-png,raf-to-webp",
 "Converting RAF to JPG happens entirely in your browser: the decoder is WebAssembly, the camera's white balance is applied, and your photos never touch a server.": "raf-to-jpg",
 "How to convert RAF to JPG": "raf-to-jpg",
