 "X-Trans sensors need dedicated demosaicing, and every renderer interprets them slightly differently. Fujifilm's own apps apply film simulations on top of raw data; ShiftRaw renders a clean, neutral interpretation with as-shot white balance — a solid base for your own grading.": "raf-to-jpg,raf-to-png,raf-to-webp",
 "Yes. GFX 50S/100S RAF files are large (100 MP from the GFX100 II) but supported — decoding just takes a few seconds longer. Memory-wise, the browser handles up to roughly 100 MP comfortably on a modern machine.": "raf-to-jpg,raf-to-png,raf-to-webp",
 "Film simulations like Classic Chrome or Acros are rendering profiles applied when Fujifilm software develops the RAF. The raw file stores only the tag of the selected simulation. ShiftRaw outputs a neutral rendering; for the simulation look, shoot JPG+RAW or use Fujifilm's app.": "raf-to-jpg,raf-to-png,raf-to-webp",
